# Conditional Logic: `if...else` 🌲

Execute code blocks conditionally based on whether an expression evaluates to truthy or falsy:

```javascript
let score = 85;

if (score >= 90) {
  console.log("Grade: A");
} else if (score >= 80) {
  console.log("Grade: B");
} else if (score >= 70) {
  console.log("Grade: C");
} else {
  console.log("Grade: Needs Improvement");
}
```

