# The `switch...case` Statement 🎯

When checking a single variable against many possible exact values, `switch` is often cleaner than a dozen `else if` statements:

```javascript
let dayNumber = 3;
let dayName;

switch (dayNumber) {
  case 1:
    dayName = "Monday";
    break;
  case 2:
    dayName = "Tuesday";
    break;
  case 3:
    dayName = "Wednesday";
    break;
  default:
    dayName = "Other day";
    break;
}

console.log("Day is:", dayName);
```

