# Intentional Switch Fallthrough 🪜

Omitting `break` intentionally allows multiple cases to share the exact same logic:

```javascript
let role = "admin";
let accessLevel;

switch (role) {
  case "admin":
  case "superadmin":
  case "owner":
    accessLevel = "Full Root Access";
    break;
  case "editor":
  case "author":
    accessLevel = "Content Editing Access";
    break;
  default:
    accessLevel = "Read Only";
    break;
}

console.log("Access Level:", accessLevel);
```

