FULL_CODE_END -->

> ⚠️ **Warning:** If the condition never becomes false, you create an **infinite loop** that crashes the browser tab or server!

# The `do...while` Loop 🔁

Unlike a `while` loop, a `do...while` loop **always executes its code block at least once**, because the condition is evaluated at the end!

```javascript
let attempts = 0;

do {
  attempts++;
  console.log(`Attempt #${attempts}`);
} while (attempts < 3);
```

