# Loop Control: `break` and `continue` 🛑

Modify the natural execution of any loop:

- **`break`**: Immediately terminates the entire loop and exits.
- **`continue`**: Skips the current iteration and jumps straight to the next one!

```javascript
console.log("Demonstrating continue (skips 3):");
for (let i = 1; i <= 5; i++) {
  if (i === 3) continue; // Skip number 3
  console.log(i);
}

console.log("Demonstrating break (stops at 3):");
for (let i = 1; i <= 5; i++) {
  if (i === 3) break; // Exit loop completely
  console.log(i);
}
```

