# Labeled Statements with `break` 🏷️

When working with nested loops, a standard `break` only terminates the innermost loop. You can label the outer loop to break out of multiple levels at once:

```javascript
outerLoop: for (let r = 0; r < 5; r++) {
  for (let c = 0; c < 5; c++) {
    if (r === 2 && c === 2) {
      console.log("Target found! Breaking outer loop.");
      break outerLoop; // Exits BOTH loops immediately!
    }
  }
}
```

