# Clean Code: The Guard Clause Pattern 🛡️

Deeply nested `if` statements create "Pyramid of Doom" code that is hard to read. Use early returns (Guard Clauses) to exit early:

```javascript
function processPayment(user, amount) {
  // Guard 1: Verify login
  if (!user.isLoggedIn) {
    return "Error: User must be logged in.";
  }
  // Guard 2: Verify funds
  if (user.balance < amount) {
    return "Error: Insufficient funds.";
  }

  // Happy path code stays un-nested and clean!
  user.balance -= amount;
  return `Payment of $${amount} successful!`;
}

console.log(processPayment({ isLoggedIn: true, balance: 100 }, 40));
```

